For a `class`, the default access specifier is `private`. For a `struct`, the default access specifier is `public`.
```cpp
class MyClass { // 'value' is private by default
    int value;
public:
    MyClass() : value(0) {}
};

struct MyStruct { // 'value' is public by default
    int value;
    MyStruct() : value(0) {}
};
```
